# the scale: on the Key page's knobs (Root, Mode: once a song, the user), not the keys (they play the Lead), nor MIDI
# in (it plays the Lead too)
wait 300
# the first piece (Timewind) is in D Aeolian; its root to C (HOME on the Berlin page, the Key page: KNOB 2, down to
# its lowest)
expect par20 5
tap HOME
wait 200
expect view 18
spin K2 -12
expect par19 0
# C Aeolian: C D Eb F G Ab Bb; the keys leave it be (E4, key 11, plays the Lead)
expect pool 0x5AD
tapkey 11
expect pool 0x5AD
# the next mode: Ionian (the Key page's KNOB 3; the modes the most common first: Aeolian, Ionian,
# Dorian, Mixolydian, pentatonic minor and major, Phrygian, Lydian)
spin K3 1
expect par20 0
expect pool 0xAB5
spin K3 -1
expect par20 5
expect pool 0x5AD
# the root up a tone: D Aeolian (the pool is relative to the root: the same)
spin K2 2
expect par19 2
expect pool 0x5AD
wait 300
shot d_aeolian.png
# pentatonic minor (four on from Aeolian)
spin K3 4
expect par20 7
expect pool 0x4A9
# MIDI in plays the Lead (any channel) and leaves the scale be: D pent min (D F G A C) stays, notes sent or not
midi 90 35 64
midi 90 37 64
wait 20
expect pool 0x4A9
midi 80 35 0
midi 80 37 0
wait 20
expect pool 0x4A9
